cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A mechanistic digital twin of Saccharomyces cerevisiae var. boulardii
  CNCM I-745
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
version: 5.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-22'
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: Niraj Sunil
    family-names: Deshmukh
    affiliation: >-
      Indian Institute of Science Education and Research (IISER) Tirupati
repository-code: 'https://github.com/nsdeshmukh306-ai/cncm-i745-digital-twin'
url: 'https://github.com/nsdeshmukh306-ai/cncm-i745-digital-twin'
abstract: >-
  Six-layer computational model of the probiotic yeast S. boulardii
  CNCM I-745. Alignment-based gene presence/absence across six genome
  assemblies drives a corrected Yeast9 genome-scale model; the central
  finding is that gene-content correction alone changes essentiality in
  zero genes and growth on one of twelve substrates. Behaviours that do
  differ are modelled explicitly: absolute transporter capacity,
  pH-dependent gastric bioenergetics, MCMC-calibrated toxin A
  proteolysis, and two-species competition with Clostridioides difficile
  under continuous dosing. Ships a FastAPI service and browser dashboard.
keywords:
  - Saccharomyces boulardii
  - CNCM I-745
  - genome-scale metabolic model
  - flux balance analysis
  - probiotic
  - Clostridioides difficile
  - digital twin
  - systems biology
references:
  - type: article
    title: 'Yeast9: a consensus yeast metabolic model'
    doi: 10.1038/s44320-024-00060-7
    scope: Base genome-scale reconstruction corrected in this work.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Complete genome sequence and comparative genomics of the probiotic
      yeast Saccharomyces boulardii
    doi: 10.1038/s41598-017-00414-2
    scope: Published gene-absence calls independently retested here.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Interpreting expression data with metabolic flux models
    doi: 10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000489
    scope: E-Flux formulation used for the zone layer.
